WEBVTT

00:00:21.350 --> 00:00:26.860
Wh-What are you waiting for?!
Hurry up and kill him! Protect me!

00:00:32.240 --> 00:00:38.410
Wh-Why?! What have I ever done to you?!

00:00:50.050 --> 00:00:55.510
William, this seems to differ
from the plan you laid out earlier.

00:00:59.890 --> 00:01:03.980
But I know you. You have
something in mind, don't you?

00:01:05.270 --> 00:01:11.440
Forgive me, Brother. This is going to
leave you exposed to denunciation.

00:01:12.530 --> 00:01:15.700
Compared to the burden you're
trying to shoulder alone,

00:01:15.700 --> 00:01:18.320
it is no trouble at all.

00:01:18.320 --> 00:01:22.240
Once you kill all of the
aristocrats on that list,

00:01:22.240 --> 00:01:26.540
many workers will lose their jobs.

00:01:26.540 --> 00:01:32.300
It is not difficult to imagine that those
men will come stampeding here.

00:01:32.300 --> 00:01:38.090
Ha, but then, I am accustomed to
dealing with that rough-mannered lot.

00:01:38.090 --> 00:01:41.510
Please leave the mansion
to me, Master William.

00:01:41.510 --> 00:01:44.730
Yes, please see to it, Jack.

00:01:44.730 --> 00:01:47.770
That will not be necessary...

00:01:47.770 --> 00:01:52.270
...if we all leave the mansion
and go into hiding.

00:01:52.270 --> 00:01:56.610
Louis, William's orders are absolute.

00:01:56.610 --> 00:02:00.120
Do not bring that up again.

00:02:01.950 --> 00:02:04.160
That's all there is to say.

00:02:07.750 --> 00:02:12.840
As of this moment...
we are beginning the final problem.

00:02:30.940 --> 00:02:35.030
<i>Tripped up by your twisted words</i>

00:02:35.030 --> 00:02:38.780
<i>I can't fall asleep at night</i>

00:02:38.780 --> 00:02:42.910
<i>Transfixed by your gaze</i>

00:02:42.910 --> 00:02:45.950
<i>I feel your sickness inside</i>

00:02:45.950 --> 00:02:50.370
<i>Injured, I break down</i>

00:02:50.370 --> 00:02:53.750
<i>this never-ending punishment</i>

00:02:53.750 --> 00:02:58.130
<i>I feel your sins all the time</i>

00:02:58.130 --> 00:03:02.720
<i>It's inescapable, take me away</i>

00:03:02.720 --> 00:03:06.310
<i>I don't feel your love</i>
<i>But I can give you love</i>

00:03:06.310 --> 00:03:10.440
<i>Show me a dream that will stir me awake</i>

00:03:10.440 --> 00:03:14.060
<i>I don't feel your love</i>
<i>But I can give you love</i>

00:03:14.060 --> 00:03:18.190
<i>Whenever I awaken, you fall apart</i>

00:03:18.190 --> 00:03:21.280
<i>Someday... (Free your soul)</i>

00:03:21.280 --> 00:03:25.620
<i>Find me (Free your mind)</i>

00:03:25.620 --> 00:03:29.080
<i>Steal your heart (Free your soul)</i>

00:03:29.080 --> 00:03:32.960
<i>Endlessly (Free your mind)</i>

00:03:32.960 --> 00:03:35.750
<i>I will scream aloud</i>

00:03:43.800 --> 00:03:49.100
"The Final Problem Act 1"

00:03:49.890 --> 00:03:55.860
What are <i>you </i>doing here?
I don't remember asking for your help.

00:03:59.530 --> 00:04:04.110
Is that any attitude for someone
who's just killed a man to have,

00:04:04.110 --> 00:04:06.370
Sherlock Holmes?

00:04:08.450 --> 00:04:12.710
That man was irredeemable dross,
who could not be apprehended.

00:04:12.710 --> 00:04:18.710
Someone had to do it. I just happened
to be the one, that's all.

00:04:18.710 --> 00:04:24.640
You're saying that you knew this would
place a heavy constraint upon you?

00:04:24.640 --> 00:04:27.680
Yeah, I knew it.

00:04:27.680 --> 00:04:32.940
I knew that if I killed him, I wouldn't be
able to pursue the Lord of Crime.

00:04:34.480 --> 00:04:36.980
Listen to me, Sherly.

00:04:36.980 --> 00:04:41.190
I'm about to tell you something
very important to you.

00:04:41.190 --> 00:04:43.110
For better or worse,

00:04:43.110 --> 00:04:48.580
you have circumstantially
committed the perfect crime.

00:04:48.580 --> 00:04:54.250
You don't mean...
they haven't found his body?!

00:04:54.250 --> 00:04:58.540
Correct. And not only were there
no eyewitnesses at the scene,

00:04:58.540 --> 00:05:01.420
because of the fire, there is no physical
evidence, such as blood traces,

00:05:01.420 --> 00:05:03.260
corroborating the crime.

00:05:04.720 --> 00:05:09.680
In other words, your statement
notwithstanding, under the circumstances,

00:05:09.680 --> 00:05:13.180
you cannot be charged with the
crime of murder on principle.

00:05:13.180 --> 00:05:14.690
What?

00:05:16.140 --> 00:05:20.400
Well, whatever the case,
Mary won't be threatened any longer,

00:05:20.400 --> 00:05:25.610
so John can safely get married.
It all worked out.

00:05:25.610 --> 00:05:27.200
Don't be ridiculous!

00:05:28.950 --> 00:05:30.530
John...

00:05:33.290 --> 00:05:35.710
When you became a killer...

00:05:35.710 --> 00:05:39.670
When you went off on your own
and sacrificed yourself for my sake...

00:05:39.670 --> 00:05:44.340
...did you actually think I would be
overjoyed because of it?!

00:05:47.340 --> 00:05:50.050
John...

00:05:50.050 --> 00:05:55.560
Even if you do get released
without having to go to trial,

00:05:55.560 --> 00:05:59.900
the moral culpability will haunt you
for the rest of your life.

00:05:59.900 --> 00:06:03.360
What kind of fetters are you going
to have to live with now?

00:06:03.360 --> 00:06:06.400
What can you possibly do about it?

00:06:06.400 --> 00:06:09.910
Reflect to yourself on that,
you thoughtless jackass!

00:06:22.340 --> 00:06:25.760
Inspector, forgive me
for disturbing your inquiry.

00:06:25.760 --> 00:06:26.880
What is it?

00:06:26.880 --> 00:06:30.180
There's significant breaking
news in the major papers!

00:06:30.180 --> 00:06:33.810
It's an article about the true
identity of the Lord of Crime!

00:06:33.810 --> 00:06:36.980
Additionally, a declaration of
responsibility from the Lord of Crime

00:06:36.980 --> 00:06:40.060
arrived here at the Yard just moments ago.

00:06:40.060 --> 00:06:42.270
A declaration of responsibility?

00:06:45.400 --> 00:06:49.490
To all the citizens of this nation,

00:06:49.490 --> 00:06:54.950
this morning, the life of Baron
Herschel was taken by me,

00:06:54.950 --> 00:07:00.500
the Lord of Crime, William James Moriarty.

00:07:00.500 --> 00:07:03.380
This is but the beginning.

00:07:03.380 --> 00:07:07.340
I hereby declare that I will
slaughter the privileged class,

00:07:07.340 --> 00:07:12.470
including the aristocracy,
that infest this nation.

00:07:15.890 --> 00:07:21.270
No one... can stop me.

00:07:22.480 --> 00:07:24.480
Lord Moriarty!

00:07:24.480 --> 00:07:26.440
Don't just stand there, answer us!

00:07:26.440 --> 00:07:31.530
Right! As head of the Moriarty family,
you have an obligation to explain this!

00:07:31.530 --> 00:07:35.990
I'll wager you actually
knew all about this!

00:07:35.990 --> 00:07:38.830
Say something, Lord Moriarty!

00:07:42.540 --> 00:07:47.250
The nobility may be one thing, but you
also killed a good man in Whiteley!

00:07:47.250 --> 00:07:50.090
Send William out here!

00:07:50.090 --> 00:07:53.260
Master William is not here!

00:07:53.260 --> 00:07:57.890
Now, unless you have business here,
I must ask you to leave!

00:07:57.890 --> 00:08:01.560
They're all reacting exactly as predicted.

00:08:01.560 --> 00:08:06.320
The nobles in Parliament are
denouncing the Moriartys,

00:08:06.320 --> 00:08:10.610
and the citizens are laying bare
their anger for the Moriartys.

00:08:11.820 --> 00:08:16.280
It's the best start to the "final problem"
that one could ask for.

00:08:16.280 --> 00:08:21.040
All this time, I've been refusing
to acknowledge...

00:08:21.040 --> 00:08:26.460
...the fact that the end of the plan
incorporated Brother's death.

00:08:30.800 --> 00:08:33.720
I've been pretending
that I did not fear it,

00:08:33.720 --> 00:08:37.180
and have been living with
my heart closed tight.

00:08:37.180 --> 00:08:42.850
But... that moment
is assuredly close at hand.

00:08:44.190 --> 00:08:47.520
Why must it be William?

00:08:47.520 --> 00:08:55.660
Why must Brother be the one who
offers his life for the world's sake?

00:08:55.660 --> 00:08:59.240
Though the world may count
Brother to be the devil...

00:09:00.290 --> 00:09:04.540
...he is all that I have.

00:09:07.750 --> 00:09:09.460
Fred...

00:09:10.840 --> 00:09:17.180
When I arrived at the mansion,
all of the servants had been knocked out.

00:09:17.180 --> 00:09:19.470
That was your doing, yes?

00:09:20.640 --> 00:09:25.890
They were only taking up arms
at their master's order.

00:09:26.810 --> 00:09:30.480
<i>This </i>is the man that should be eliminated.

00:09:30.480 --> 00:09:33.820
But, William, you are different!

00:09:33.820 --> 00:09:41.030
You are only executing judgment
that no one else can! And yet...

00:09:41.030 --> 00:09:45.750
...you are actually willing to die
to take responsibility for this!

00:09:49.170 --> 00:09:51.920
Justice, is it?

00:10:07.140 --> 00:10:11.110
Truthfully, I don't enjoy
smoking, you know.

00:10:11.110 --> 00:10:13.820
It pollutes the lungs.

00:10:14.780 --> 00:10:20.570
I don't consider the actions I'm taking
to be in the name of justice.

00:10:20.570 --> 00:10:25.910
I've never believed that a person has
the right to pass judgment on another.

00:10:25.910 --> 00:10:27.250
Huh?

00:10:28.580 --> 00:10:32.130
No matter how heinous the person was,

00:10:32.130 --> 00:10:36.670
I am cognizant of the ever-accumulating
offences I am committing.

00:10:38.720 --> 00:10:42.350
My scarlet-stained hands...

00:10:42.350 --> 00:10:48.100
There is no way, no matter
what I do, to rub this stain out.

00:10:49.770 --> 00:10:52.560
So you see, Fred...

00:10:53.820 --> 00:10:58.400
...I'm more than ready to die already.

00:11:02.910 --> 00:11:07.000
There's no way I can stop him on my own.

00:11:08.000 --> 00:11:12.420
At this point, all I can do
is appeal to <i>him</i>.

00:11:18.050 --> 00:11:22.010
Do you intend to betray Brother, Fred?

00:11:28.310 --> 00:11:30.770
I see.

00:11:30.770 --> 00:11:33.610
That's what Brother said.

00:11:33.610 --> 00:11:39.860
I'll accept any punishment,
but I can't go along with William dying--

00:11:39.860 --> 00:11:43.450
with William <i>wanting </i>to die.

00:11:45.660 --> 00:11:47.200
I agree.

00:11:47.200 --> 00:11:48.540
Huh?

00:11:53.080 --> 00:11:55.340
I hate to admit it,

00:11:55.340 --> 00:12:00.220
but it will not be possible for us to
intervene without ruining the plan.

00:12:00.220 --> 00:12:05.300
It will be the first time I've ever
gone against William.

00:12:05.300 --> 00:12:11.480
Still, if there's a chance
of saving his life...

00:12:11.480 --> 00:12:16.650
...then I will have no regrets,
even if it means betraying him.

00:12:21.320 --> 00:12:23.360
M-Mo--

00:12:23.360 --> 00:12:25.530
Moriarty...!

00:12:30.830 --> 00:12:34.540
I-Is anybody there?! Anybody?!

00:12:45.640 --> 00:12:50.310
You hide behind children?
You could not be more despicable.

00:12:50.310 --> 00:12:54.140
Go ahead and do it, if you dare, Moriarty!

00:13:00.900 --> 00:13:02.690
Huh?

00:13:02.690 --> 00:13:06.240
You can-- You can take my life!

00:13:06.240 --> 00:13:10.290
So please, spare my father and brother!

00:13:11.290 --> 00:13:13.120
I beg you!

00:13:14.160 --> 00:13:16.210
I beg you!

00:13:32.980 --> 00:13:35.980
F-Father...

00:13:35.980 --> 00:13:37.690
Father!

00:13:41.570 --> 00:13:47.110
I trampled down your resolve
to stake your own life.

00:13:47.110 --> 00:13:51.830
I believe myself deserving of
being killed by you, right here.

00:13:51.830 --> 00:13:59.790
However, cowardly though it may sound,
I cannot afford to die just yet.

00:13:59.790 --> 00:14:04.670
You'll pay for this...
I swear you'll pay for this...

00:14:04.670 --> 00:14:07.840
Moriarty!

00:14:12.850 --> 00:14:20.520
William, no longer... can I even
pull the trigger on your behalf.

00:14:21.610 --> 00:14:25.320
The only one who can save you now...

00:14:40.790 --> 00:14:44.050
William James Moriarty...

00:14:45.170 --> 00:14:48.680
A past judgment in favour
of a child from the slums...

00:14:48.680 --> 00:14:52.220
That was Liam. I know it.

00:14:52.220 --> 00:14:56.480
After that, he and his brother were
taken in by the Moriartys' oldest son,

00:14:56.480 --> 00:15:00.850
became adoptees... then using
the occasion of the estate fire,

00:15:00.850 --> 00:15:03.820
he took the place of
the second son, William.

00:15:03.820 --> 00:15:07.950
Which means that all three brothers
are co-conspirators from the start.

00:15:07.950 --> 00:15:11.110
All three are the Lord of Crime.

00:15:11.110 --> 00:15:13.370
In the incident aboard the <i>Noahtic</i>,

00:15:13.370 --> 00:15:16.950
I caught Liam's eye when
I happened to be around.

00:15:16.950 --> 00:15:21.290
He tested me during the Drebber case,
to see if I would be useful to him.

00:15:22.960 --> 00:15:26.380
The hidden agenda in all of these cases,

00:15:26.380 --> 00:15:29.800
as seen from the fact that Liam
is playing Robin Hood...

00:15:29.800 --> 00:15:34.760
The dots are now at last becoming
connected in my head.

00:15:35.760 --> 00:15:41.770
There's a single red thread...
behind all of these cases!

00:15:49.320 --> 00:15:54.530
And now, I am standing
on the same level that he is.

00:16:02.420 --> 00:16:06.040
Is that right? Even Marquis Glover?

00:16:06.040 --> 00:16:09.340
It seems that the Lord of Crime
does indeed mean to destroy

00:16:09.340 --> 00:16:12.720
the privileged class of this country.

00:16:12.720 --> 00:16:17.180
This is likely a message to us
from the Lord of Crime,

00:16:17.180 --> 00:16:23.100
telling us that he can easily kill anyone,
anywhere, at any time.

00:16:23.100 --> 00:16:28.940
Director Holmes,
bring Sherlock Holmes here at once.

00:16:30.150 --> 00:16:31.780
Yes, Your Majesty.

00:16:49.710 --> 00:16:53.130
I'm sorry, John.

00:16:53.130 --> 00:16:59.600
In my own way, my intention was to act
with your feelings foremost in mind.

00:16:59.600 --> 00:17:03.600
I wasn't concerned with what
would happen to me.

00:17:03.600 --> 00:17:06.900
But a little--no...

00:17:06.900 --> 00:17:10.570
...a <i>lot </i>more thought
should have gone into this.

00:17:10.570 --> 00:17:16.490
Just as I have a need for you,
you have a need for me.

00:17:16.490 --> 00:17:18.870
As long as I have someone like that,

00:17:18.870 --> 00:17:22.700
I should be much more
careful about myself.

00:17:22.700 --> 00:17:28.250
From now on, I promise,
I will treat myself much better.

00:17:34.930 --> 00:17:36.720
Look up at me.

00:17:38.430 --> 00:17:42.390
There's something that I, too,
need to say to you.

00:17:43.350 --> 00:17:50.690
Thank you, for saving Mary,
and for saving us, Sherlock.

00:17:50.690 --> 00:17:52.400
John...

00:17:54.400 --> 00:17:59.660
Well, let's be off, Sherlock.
Her Majesty awaits us.

00:17:59.660 --> 00:18:02.870
Yeah. Thank you, John.

00:18:04.080 --> 00:18:07.040
Before we go, though, you need a necktie.

00:18:10.630 --> 00:18:16.050
Thank you both for coming
in our nation's time of need.

00:18:16.050 --> 00:18:21.470
Sherlock Holmes, and Dr John H. Watson.

00:18:21.470 --> 00:18:25.520
It is an honour to make your
acquaintance, Your Majesty.

00:18:36.490 --> 00:18:39.280
That was bold of you, Sherly.

00:18:44.370 --> 00:18:47.960
This situation that Liam has
risked his life to create

00:18:47.960 --> 00:18:51.210
is an opportunity that
will not come again.

00:18:51.210 --> 00:18:56.050
If things do not change now, then one way
or another, this country is finished.

00:18:56.050 --> 00:19:01.760
Hmm, so it seems that you have
realised his design, as well.

00:19:03.260 --> 00:19:06.100
Then you understood him, too?

00:19:09.020 --> 00:19:10.690
Good-bye.

00:19:17.110 --> 00:19:19.950
Don't get yourself killed, Sherly.

00:19:28.460 --> 00:19:30.370
Miss Hudson...

00:19:32.080 --> 00:19:34.800
Welcome home, Sherlock.

00:19:36.340 --> 00:19:38.050
I'm back.

00:19:40.300 --> 00:19:44.760
By the way, a telegram
arrived earlier for you.

00:20:04.070 --> 00:20:07.200
The third son of the
Moriarty family, Louis...

00:20:07.200 --> 00:20:11.670
And you're the one who was disguised
as the old woman during the Hope affair.

00:20:11.670 --> 00:20:12.920
Your name is...

00:20:12.920 --> 00:20:15.380
Fred Porlock.

00:20:17.000 --> 00:20:20.300
There is only one reason why I would call
you out in this manner. The truth is--

00:20:20.300 --> 00:20:23.970
You want me to save Liam's life, yes?

00:20:26.640 --> 00:20:30.100
In order for Liam's plan to
achieve its greatest effect,

00:20:30.100 --> 00:20:32.730
it is necessary for the
Lord of Crime to die.

00:20:33.690 --> 00:20:38.690
And the timing of the two of you
contacting me like this must mean...

00:20:38.690 --> 00:20:44.530
...that Liam is not going to feign
his death; he actually means to die.

00:20:44.530 --> 00:20:47.700
None of that pretence matters! You will...

00:20:47.700 --> 00:20:50.750
I intend to save Liam.

00:20:51.660 --> 00:20:55.250
As his... friend...

00:20:59.170 --> 00:21:03.470
That's all I can say right now.
Is that good enough?

00:21:06.550 --> 00:21:09.600
You've actually reassured me--

00:21:09.600 --> 00:21:13.390
by being a genuine
flesh-and-blood organisation.

00:21:13.390 --> 00:21:19.980
Mr Holmes, we are prepared
to accept any punishment. So...

00:21:19.980 --> 00:21:23.150
...please make sure to save my brother.

00:21:25.280 --> 00:21:27.200
Leave him to me.

00:21:28.370 --> 00:21:35.670
<i>Fate that over time changes</i>
<i>into chains of sorrow,</i>

00:21:35.670 --> 00:21:43.880
<i>leave me the light of rebirth</i>
<i>for the world ahead</i>

00:21:50.510 --> 00:21:54.480
<i>Struck by a frustration</i>
<i>I'd never experienced before,</i>

00:21:54.480 --> 00:21:57.860
<i>I feel lost, I feel lost</i>

00:21:57.860 --> 00:22:01.860
<i>The letters I dashed off</i>
<i>are all I remember</i>

00:22:01.860 --> 00:22:05.240
<i>It's all true, it's all true</i>

00:22:05.240 --> 00:22:12.660
<i>Witness as I forgo my forsaken future</i>
<i>with no regrets</i>

00:22:12.660 --> 00:22:21.250
<i>and you will win your intent</i>
<i>at the expense of becoming my pawn</i>

00:22:23.260 --> 00:22:29.050
<i>A scarlet thread fluttering in the wind</i>
<i>at five in the morning</i>

00:22:29.050 --> 00:22:35.310
<i>I'll recover my memories on the last day</i>

00:22:35.310 --> 00:22:38.100
<i>Hold me down till the end</i>

00:22:38.100 --> 00:22:43.780
<i>Finish by wiping away my sins,</i>

00:22:43.780 --> 00:22:50.450
<i>warning me to stay true if I desire beauty</i>

00:23:28.400 --> 00:23:33.990
Can I ask you to take this tale--
the tale of Sherlock Holmes's nemesis--

00:23:33.990 --> 00:23:37.450
and bring it to a close?

00:23:37.450 --> 00:23:39.460
Of course.

00:23:47.050 --> 00:23:52.340
Next time on <i>Moriarty the Patriot</i>:
"The Final Problem Act 2."
